        {
          "day": 2,
          "number": 9,
          "problem": "Choose distinct positive integers $X_1,\\ldots,X_n$ sequentially as follows: $X_1=i$ with probability $2^{-i}$. Once $X_1,\\ldots,X_j$ are selected, list the unused positive integers in increasing order $u_1<u_2<\\cdots$ and set $X_{j+1}=u_i$ with conditional probability $2^{-i}$. For $Y_n=\\max(X_1,\\ldots,X_n)$, prove $\\mathbb E(Y_n)=\\sum_{i=1}^{n}\\frac{2^i}{2^i-1}$.",
